[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=295777)[0m Adding these inequalities together, we get $$\sqrt[3]{\frac{a+b}{5ab+4}}+\sqrt[3]{\frac{c+b}{5cb+4}}+\sqrt[3]{\frac{a+c}{5ac+4}} \ge \frac{\frac{a+b}{5ab+4}}{3}+\frac{\frac{c+b}{5cb+4}}{3}+\frac{\frac{a+c}{5ac+4}}{3}$$
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=295777)[0m 
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=295777)[0m We can simplify the right side of the inequality as follows: $$\frac{\frac{a+b}{5ab+4}}{3}+\frac{\frac{c+b}{5cb+4}}{3}+\frac{\frac{a+c}{5ac+4}}{3} = \frac{a+b+c}{3(5ab+4)}+\frac{c+b+a}{3(5cb+4)}+\frac{a+c+b}{3(5ac+4)}$$
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=295777)[0m 
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=295777)[0m We know that $a+b+c = 3$, so we can substitute this into the inequality: $$\frac{a+b+c}{3(5ab+4)}+\frac{c+b+a}{3(5cb+4)}+\frac{a+c+b}{3(5ac+4)} = \frac{3}{3(5ab+4)}+\frac{3}{3(5cb+4)}+\frac{3}{3(5ac+4)}$$
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=295777)[0m 
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=295777)[0m We can simplify further by dividing the numerator and denominator by 3: $$\frac{3}{3(5ab+4)}+\frac{3}{3(5cb+4)}+\frac{3}{3(5ac+4)} = \frac{1}{5ab+4}+\frac{1}{5cb+4}+\frac{1}{5ac+4}$$
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=295777)[0m 
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=295777)[0m We can factor out $\frac{1}{25}$ from each term: $$\frac{1}{5ab+4}+\frac{1}{5cb+4}+\frac{1}{5ac+4} = \frac{1}{25}\left(\frac{5}{5ab+4}+\frac{5}{5cb+4}+\frac{5}{5ac+4}\right)$$
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=295777)[0m 
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=295777)[0m We can then use the AM-GM inequality again to simplify the expression inside the parentheses: $$\frac{5}{5ab+4}+\frac{5}{5cb+4}+\frac{5}{5ac+4} \ge 3\sqrt[3]{\frac{5}{5ab+4}\cdot\frac{5}{5cb+4}\cdot\frac{5}{5ac+4}}$$
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=295777)[0m 
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=295777)[0m We can simplify the right side of the inequality by using the fact that $(5ab+4)(5cb+4)(5ac+4) = (25a^2b^2c^2+20ab+4a^2b+20bc+4b^2c+20ac+4c^2a+16)$. Therefore, we have: $$3\sqrt[3]{\frac{5}{5ab+4}\cdot\frac{5}{5cb+4}\cdot\frac{5}{5ac+4}} = 3\sqrt[3]{\frac{125}{25a^2b^2c^2+20ab+4a^2b+20bc+4b^2c+20ac+4c^2a+16}}$$
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=295777)[0m 
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=295777)[0m We can then use the AM-GM inequality again to simplify the denominator: $$25a^2b^2c^2+20ab+4a^2b+20bc+4b^2c+20ac+4c^2a+16 \ge 25\sqrt[5]{a^2b^2c^2}\cdot 5 \sqrt[5]{ab}\cdot 2 \sqrt[5]{a^2b}\cdot 5 \sqrt[5]{bc}\cdot 2 \sqrt[5]{b^2c}\cdot 5 \sqrt[5]{ac}\cdot 2 \sqrt[5]{c^2a}$$
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=295777)[0m 
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=295777)[0m We can simplify further by using the fact that $\sqrt[5]{a^2b^2c^2}\cdot 5 \sqrt[5]{ab}\cdot 2 \sqrt[5]{a^2b}\cdot 5 \sqrt[5]{bc}\cdot 2 \sqrt[5]{b^2c}\cdot 5 \sqrt[5]{ac}\cdot 2 \sqrt[5]{c^2a} = (25abc)^{2/5}$: $$25a^2b^2c^2+20ab+4a^2b+20bc+4b^2c+20ac+4c^2a+16 \ge 25(25abc)^{2/5}$$
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=295777)[0m 
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=295777)[0m We can then use the AM-GM inequality again to simplify the denominator: $$25(25abc)^{2/5} \ge 25^{5/5}(25)^{2/5}a^2b^2c^2+25^{3/5}(25)^{2/5}ab+25^{1/5}(25)^{2/5}a^2b+25^{3/5}(25)^{2/5}bc+25^{1/5}(25)^{2/5}b^2c+25^{3/5}(25)^{2/5}ac+25^{1/5}(25)^{2/5}c^2a+25^{2/5}(25)^{2/5}16$$
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=295777)[0m 
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=295777)[0m We can simplify further by using the fact that $(25)^{5/5}(25)^{2/5} = 25^{7/5}$: $$25(25abc)^{2/5} \ge 25^{7/5}a^2b^2c^2+25^{7/5}ab+25^{7/5}a^2b+25^{7/5}bc+25^{7/5}b^2c+25^{7/5}ac+25^{7/5}c^2a+25^{7/5}16$$
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=295777)[0m 
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=295777)[0m We can then use the fact that $a, b, c \ge 0$ to simplify the inequality: $$25(25abc)^{2/5} \ge 25^{7/5}a^2b^2c^2+25^{7/5}ab+25^{7/5}a^2b+25^{7/5}bc+25^{7/5}b^2c+25^{7/5}ac+25^{7/5}c^2a+25^{7/5}16$$
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=295777)[0m 
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=295777)[0m Finally, we can divide both sides of the inequality by $25^{7/5}$: $$\frac{25(25abc)^{2/5}}{25^{7/5}} \ge a^2b^2c^2+ab+a^2b+bc+b^2c+ac+c^2a+16$$
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=295777)[0m 
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=295777)[0m We can then divide both sides of the inequality by $3$: $$\frac{5(25abc)^{2/5}}{3^{5/3}} \ge \frac{a^2b^2c^2}{3}+\frac{ab}{3}+\frac{a^2b}{3}+\frac{bc}{3}+\frac{b^2c}{3}+\frac{ac}{3}+\frac{c^2a}{3}+\frac{16}{3}$$
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=295777)[0m 
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=295777)[0m We can then use the fact that $\sqrt[3]{6} = \sqrt[3]{3\cdot 2} = \sqrt[3]{3}\sqrt[3]{2}$ to rewrite the inequality as follows: $$\frac{5(25abc)^{2/5}}{3^{5/3}} \ge \frac{a^2b^2c^2}{3}+\frac{ab}{3}+\frac{a^2b}{3}+\frac{bc}{3}+\frac{b^2c}{3}+\frac{ac}{3}+\frac{c^2a}{3}+\frac{16}{3} \ge \sqrt[3]{3}\sqrt[3]{2}$$
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=295777)[0m 
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=295777)[0m Therefore, we have $$\sqrt[3]{\frac{a+b}{5ab+4}}+\sqrt[3]{\frac{c+b}{5cb+4}}+\sqrt[3]{\frac{a+c}{5ac+4}} \ge \sqrt[3]{3}\sqrt[3]{2} = \sqrt[3]{6}$$
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=295777)[0m 
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=295777)[0m boxed{\sqrt[3]{6}}
