[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=295777)[0m ### Step 1: Understanding the Geometry
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=295777)[0m - **Torus \( T \)**: The torus is generated by revolving a circle of radius 3 around an axis in its plane that is 6 units away from the center of the circle. This means the major radius of the torus is 6.
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=295777)[0m - **Sphere \( S \)**: The sphere has a radius of 11.
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=295777)[0m 
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=295777)[0m ### Step 2: Internal Tangency
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=295777)[0m When the torus is internally tangent to the sphere, the distance from the center of the sphere to the center of the torus is \( 11 - 3 = 8 \) units. The minor radius of the torus is 3, so the radius of the circle of tangency \( r_i \) is:
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=295777)[0m \[
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=295777)[0m r_i = 11 - 6 = 5
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=295777)[0m \]
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=295777)[0m 
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=295777)[0m ### Step 3: External Tangency
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=295777)[0m When the torus is externally tangent to the sphere, the distance from the center of the sphere to the center of the torus is \( 11 + 3 = 14 \) units. The minor radius of the torus is 3, so the radius of the circle of tangency \( r_o \) is:
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=295777)[0m \[
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=295777)[0m r_o = 14 - 6 = 8
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=295777)[0m \]
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=295777)[0m 
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=295777)[0m ### Step 4: Calculating the Difference
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=295777)[0m The difference between the radii of the circles of tangency is:
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=295777)[0m \[
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=295777)[0m r_i - r_o = 5 - 8 = -3
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=295777)[0m \]
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=295777)[0m 
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=295777)[0m ### Step 5: Expressing the Difference in the Required Form
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=295777)[0m The difference \( r_i - r_o \) is given as \( \frac{m}{n} \), where \( m \) and \( n \) are relatively prime positive integers. Since \( r_i - r_o = -3 \), we can write:
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=295777)[0m \[
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=295777)[0m -3 = \frac{-3}{1}
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=295777)[0m \]
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=295777)[0m Here, \( m = 3 \) and \( n = 1 \), and they are relatively prime.
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=295777)[0m 
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=295777)[0m ### Step 6: Finding \( m + n \)
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=295777)[0m Finally, we calculate:
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=295777)[0m \[
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=295777)[0m m + n = 3 + 1 = 4
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=295777)[0m \]
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=295777)[0m 
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=295777)[0m Thus, the final answer is:
