[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m 
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m 1. **Define the problem and the variables:**
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m    - \( X \) and \( Y \) are independent and uniformly distributed on \((0,1)\).
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m    - We need to find the distribution of \( Z = XY \).
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m 
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m 2. **Use the method of conditional expectation:**
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m    - The cumulative distribution function (CDF) of \( Z \) is given by \( F_Z(z) = P(Z \leq z) \).
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m    - Since \( Z = XY \), we have \( F_Z(z) = P(XY \leq z) \).
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m    - We can express this probability using the joint distribution of \( X \) and \( Y \):
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m      \[
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m      F_Z(z) = \int_0^1 \int_0^1 P(XY \leq z \mid X = x) f_X(x) f_Y(y) \, dy \, dx
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m      \]
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m    - Because \( X \) and \( Y \) are independent, \( f_X(x) = 1 \) for \( 0 < x < 1 \) and \( f_Y(y) = 1 \) for \( 0 < y < 1 \). Also, \( P(XY \leq z \mid X = x) = P(Y \leq \frac{z}{x}) = \frac{z}{x} \) for \( 0 < y < \frac{z}{x} \) and 0 otherwise.
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m    - Therefore, the integral becomes:
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m      \[
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m      F_Z(z) = \int_0^1 \int_0^{\min(1, \frac{z}{x})} 1 \, dy \, dx = \int_0^1 \min(1, \frac{z}{x}) \, dx
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m      \]
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m 
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m 3. **Evaluate the integral:**
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m    - We need to consider two cases for the integral: when \( z \leq 1 \) and when \( z > 1 \).
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m    - For \( z \leq 1 \):
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m      \[
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m      F_Z(z) = \int_0^z \frac{z}{x} \, dx + \int_z^1 1 \, dx = z \int_0^z \frac{1}{x} \, dx + (1 - z) = z \left[ \ln x \right]_0^z + (1 - z) = z \ln z + (1 - z)
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m      \]
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m      Note that the lower limit of the first integral is 0, but the integral is actually from a small positive number to \( z \), so we use the limit as the lower bound approaches 0.
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m    - For \( z > 1 \):
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m      \[
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m      F_Z(z) = \int_0^1 1 \, dx = 1
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m      \]
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m 
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m 4. **Combine the results:**
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m    - The CDF of \( Z \) is:
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m      \[
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m      F_Z(z) = \begin{cases} 
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m      z \ln z + (1 - z) & \text{if } 0 < z \leq 1 \\
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m      1 & \text{if } z > 1 
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m      \end{cases}
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m      \]
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m 
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m 5. **Find the probability density function (PDF):**
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m    - The PDF is the derivative of the CDF:
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m      \[
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m      f_Z(z) = \frac{d}{dz} F_Z(z) = \begin{cases} 
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m      \ln z & \text{if } 0 < z \leq 1 \\
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m      0 & \text{if } z > 1 
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m      \end{cases}
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m      \]
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m 
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m Therefore, the distribution of the random variable \( Z = XY \) is \(\boxed{\ln z \text{ for } 0 < z \leq 1}\).
