[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m 1. **Define the problem and the variables:**
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m    \( X \) and \( Y \) are independent and uniformly distributed on \((0,1)\). We need to find the distribution of \( Z = XY \).
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m 
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m 2. **Use the transformation method:**
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m    Since \( X \) and \( Y \) are independent, the joint density function of \( X \) and \( Y \) is \( f_{X,Y}(x,y) = f_X(x) f_Y(y) = 1 \) for \( 0 < x < 1 \) and \( 0 < y < 1 \).
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m 
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m 3. **Find the cumulative distribution function (CDF) of \( Z \):**
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m    The CDF of \( Z \) is given by \( F_Z(z) = P(Z \leq z) = P(XY \leq z) \). We can express this probability as a double integral over the region where \( xy \leq z \):
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m    \[
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m    F_Z(z) = \int_0^1 \int_0^{\min(1, z/x)} 1 \, dy \, dx
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m    \]
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m    The inner integral is \( \int_0^{\min(1, z/x)} 1 \, dy = \min(1, z/x) \). Therefore, we need to consider two cases: \( 0 < z \leq 1 \) and \( z > 1 \).
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m 
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m 4. **Evaluate the CDF for \( 0 < z \leq 1 \):**
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m    \[
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m    F_Z(z) = \int_0^z \frac{z}{x} \, dx + \int_z^1 1 \, dx = z \int_0^z \frac{1}{x} \, dx + (1 - z) = z \ln z + 1 - z
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m    \]
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m    For \( z > 1 \), the region where \( xy \leq z \) is the entire unit square, so:
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m    \[
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m    F_Z(z) = 1
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m    \]
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m 
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m 5. **Combine the results to get the CDF:**
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m    \[
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m    F_Z(z) = \begin{cases} 
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m    0 & \text{if } z \leq 0 \\
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m    z \ln z + 1 - z & \text{if } 0 < z \leq 1 \\
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m    1 & \text{if } z > 1 
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m    \end{cases}
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m    \]
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m 
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m 6. **Find the probability density function (PDF) by differentiating the CDF:**
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m    \[
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m    f_Z(z) = \frac{d}{dz} F_Z(z) = \begin{cases} 
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m    0 & \text{if } z \leq 0 \text{ or } z > 1 \\
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m    \ln z + 1 - 1 = \ln z & \text{if } 0 < z \leq 1 
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m    \end{cases}
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m    \]
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m    Therefore, the PDF of \( Z \) is:
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m    \[
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m    f_Z(z) = \begin{cases} 
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m    \ln z & \text{if } 0 < z \leq 1 \\
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m    0 & \text{otherwise} 
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m    \end{cases}
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m    \]
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m 
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m The final answer is:
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m \[
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m \boxed{\ln z \text{ for } 0 < z \leq 1}
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-2) pid=295776)[0m \]
